From 79179dba7712b54a7f0252a75eae093935a0477c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: keptn42 <keptn42@noreply.codeberg.org>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 09:06:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] moe_gemm_q decode form: two K blocks a pass, and weight
 loads without serial waits

In the decode form every weight load is a flat_load through a table pointer
in VGPRs, and the waitcnt pass puts s_wait_loadcnt 0 in front of each, so a
pass's scale, activation and weight loads go out one after the other.
R4D_MOE_UWLOAD=1 makes the table entries uniform and reads them through
address_space(1), issues the scale loads unconditionally, and uses LDS
barriers in the K loop with one release fence for the prefetch: one wait a
pass. R4D_MOE_GU_FK256=1 (or =N, up to N routed rows) stages two 128-wide
K blocks a gate_up pass. Both bit-identical and off by default; the default
kernels are instruction-identical to before. r4d_selftest compares every
variant byte for byte.
