From 96456cbe09da9689fe1bd73d1d569522830b4e04 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: keptn42 <keptn42@noreply.codeberg.org>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 09:07:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] moe_gemm_q decode form: the block's run in one round trip

A decode-form block finds its run by a chunked search: four to six
dependent L2 round trips and two barriers a chunk, paid also by blocks that
find nothing. R4D_MOE_RUNSCAN=1 loads the block's sorted rows and all
offsets in one batch, numbers the runs in expert order with a DPP scan, and
hands the run's bounds over LDS. Up to 512 experts; above that the chunked
search runs. Bit-identical, off by default. Flash-Next at tp 4 with UW and
RS: 36.9 -> 36.1 ms a step at 16 concurrent.
